CAVEATS
  * You can only have one libtorch per process: always `source namd_benchmarks/env.sh`, and keep LIBTORCH_ROOT and NAMD_MLFF_LIB paired
    (env.sh does this). Don't prepend another torch/lib to LD_LIBRARY_PATH for NAMD runs.
  * If you switch LIBTORCH_ROOT, use a FRESH shell (or `unset NAMD_MLFF_LIB` first). NAMD_MLFF_LIB is now sticky once exported, so
    re-sourcing env.sh would keep the old shim while LD_LIBRARY_PATH leads with the new libtorch -> mixed-libtorch failures.
  * MULTI-WALKER IS BROKEN (walk>=2, bug in the NAMD code, NOT caused by libtorch): the batch server partition segfaults as soon as a client
    connects ("MLFF client: server closed before sending its capability word" / "failed to read energy"). I reproduced it on CPU
    with the OLD stack (namd3.libtorch2.6.bak + libtorch 2.6 + old shim), and namd3.prefix_bak (Jun 5 build) works on CPU. So the
    regression is in the Jul-31 namd3 source (ComputeMLFF.C PBC/protocol changes). walk0 and walk1 work. I have not patched it.
  * The colvars torchann component was recompiled against 2.11 but not exercised.
